191
00:09:54,160 --> 00:10:00,560
So now we're going to take a look at three short phrases that we've picked out for you on Fluency Builder.

192
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:00,800
Fluency Builder.

193
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:08,360
So this first phrase is something that we almost always say with our friends or family when we're hungry, we're shopping.

194
00:10:09,260 --> 00:10:11,800
Sometimes you're outside and you just really want to eat.

195
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:14,520
You say, hey, let's grab a bite to eat.

196
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:15,280
That's right.

197
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:22,040
It's a very natural colloquial way of saying, let's go get something to eat or let's go eat something.

198
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:25,600
So it could be small, it could be a snack like an ice cream, but it can also be dinner.

199
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:28,020
So hey, do you want to go grab a bite to eat sometime?

200
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:30,960
That means, hey, you want to go have lunch or dinner sometime?

201
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:31,170
Very good.

202
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:35,650
So the phrase is grab a bite or go grab a bite to eat.

203
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:45,770
So a bite can be a noun, like a thing, like a piece of food that you eat, but it can also be a verb, to bite, like the dog bites the man.

204
00:10:46,310 --> 00:10:47,350
And so you have to be careful with this one.

205
00:10:47,470 --> 00:10:48,510
In this case, it's a noun.

206
00:10:48,910 --> 00:10:49,730
Okay, very good.

207
00:10:50,290 --> 00:10:56,450
And well, she wanted to first go to the store and she said, I want to pick up a few things.

208
00:10:56,980 --> 00:11:01,760
Well, usually when you pick something up, you take it from a table or from the ground.

209
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:07,140
But in this case, it means to buy something because you can't just pick something up in a store and then walk away.

210
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:08,020
You have to pay for it.

211
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:13,560
So for example, you can say, when you come home, can you pick up a carton of milk?

212
00:11:14,190 --> 00:11:16,630
So that means, can you buy some milk on your way home?

213
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:19,880
It doesn't mean, can you take some from someone else or steal some.

214
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:20,880
Exactly.

215
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:26,600
All right, so to pick something up, to buy, to go and get, but obviously you have to pay.

216
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:33,680
All right, and he used this very interesting phrase when she was getting all these things for her.

217
