Why don't we go back, listen to our dialogue for the last time and we'll be back in a bit.

238
00:12:30,230 --> 00:12:31,010
I'm hungry.

239
00:12:31,230 --> 00:12:32,330
Let's go grab a bite to eat.

240
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:33,450
Yeah, me too.

241
00:12:34,090 --> 00:12:36,510
Oh, can we stop at the shop really fast?

242
00:12:37,290 --> 00:12:40,750
I lost my makeup bag at the airport and I want to pick up a few things.

243
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:41,770
Will you take long?

244
00:12:42,190 --> 00:12:43,590
No, five minutes.

245
00:12:43,910 --> 00:12:44,230
I promise.

246
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:50,820
Come on, we've been here for almost an hour.

247
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:52,920
I thought you said you're only going to get a few things.

248
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:56,160
How long does it take you to pick out a lipstick and some nail polish?

249
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:57,060
Are you crazy?

250
00:12:57,900 --> 00:12:59,840
You have no idea what you're talking about.

251
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:07,160
As for my eyes, I have to get eyeliner and eyelash curler, eye shadow, an eyebrow pencil and mascara.

252
00:13:07,230 --> 00:13:09,630
Then I need to get foundation, liquid foundation.

253
00:13:10,490 --> 00:13:11,630
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

254
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:12,210
Are you nuts?

255
00:13:12,970 --> 00:13:14,250
How much is all this going to cost?

256
00:13:14,890 --> 00:13:17,310
I'm looking at the price of each one of these little things and it's outrageous.

257
00:13:18,170 --> 00:13:19,670
This is basically a crayon.

258
00:13:20,070 --> 00:13:20,850
What about you?

259
00:13:21,390 --> 00:13:26,050
You spend as much money or more on your razors, aftershave, cologne and gel.

260
00:13:26,830 --> 00:13:29,190
Not to mention how much you spend on clothes and-

261
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:31,350
Fine, get the stupid $30 crayon.

262
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:42,350
All right, so talking about makeup, a lot of things here.

263
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:44,400
Maybe I didn't mention a couple of things.

264
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:46,040
I don't know.

265
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:49,480
We took a look at the most important things, I think, right?

266
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:53,360
But you also mentioned something, for example, cover-up.

267
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:55,440
There's something, such makeup called cover-up.

268
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:57,320
Yeah, so cover-up.

269
00:13:57,320 --> 00:14:04,210
It could be a couple of different things in English, for example, something that you wear to cover your body when you're at the beach.

270
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:07,550
You don't want to walk around and everyone can see you in your bathing suit.

271
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:15,610
But when we're talking about makeup, a cover-up is a thing that we use to hide blemishes or zits or pimples.

272
00:14:15,850 --> 00:14:21,930
You know when you get a really small red dot on your face and you're embarrassed and it's ugly, and you don't want anyone to see it?

273
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:29,000
Well, cover-up is a kind of makeup you use that looks like your skin color and you put it on top and you can't see the red anymore.

274
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,690
Okay, so you cover up your pimple.

275
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,160
Yeah, or you use cover-up.

276
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:34,630
It's a noun too.

277
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:40,550
Okay, and I've also seen that, well, many girls don't really wear too much lipstick anymore nowadays.

278
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,750
They use this thing called lip gloss.

279
00:14:43,250 --> 00:14:44,190
Okay, lip gloss.

280
00:14:44,770 --> 00:14:46,910
Remember we were talking about polish earlier?

281
00:14:47,610 --> 00:14:49,090
Well, gloss is a similar word.

282
00:14:49,210 --> 00:14:51,910
It means something that makes another thing shiny.

283
00:14:52,720 --> 00:15:02,480
And so lipstick can be very dry, can be very flat, but lip gloss is something that makes things look wet, makes things look shiny.

284
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:12,280
Okay, and actually one last thing before, when we talked about gel, I guess guys use gel but women use this thing called mousse.

285
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,160
Or they could use gel too.

286
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:16,760
I don't think it's gender specific, but a lot of people use mousse.

287
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:19,080
I know some men who use mousse as well.

288
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,720
Mousse is kind of like a foam.

289
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:23,160
You know it comes in a can and it goes ffff.

290
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:26,110
Yeah, and it inflates this white substance.

291
00:15:26,430 --> 00:15:28,910
Yeah, it looks like, I don't know.

292
00:15:29,170 --> 00:15:29,650
Like whipped cream.

293
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:31,280
Like whipped cream, yeah.

294
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:32,350
And you put it in your hair and it's very fluffy.

295
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:34,990
And it's actually less strong.

296
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:38,870
It's not like gel because if you put it in your hair, your hair won't look hard.

297
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:43,720
But it will help shape your hair if you want to keep your hair in one place.

298
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:44,780
A lot of things here.

299
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:48,840
I think in beauty and cosmetics, we have a lot of a lot of things.

300
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:52,720
And probably we didn't even touch on half of the things that are out there.

301
00:15:52,720 --> 00:16:02,060
So if you have any questions or if you want to ask us anything at all about this lesson or anything else, you can always come to EnglishPod.com and leave your questions and comments there.

302
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:04,840
So we'll see you at EnglishPod and until next time.

303
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:13,218
Alright, bye everyone!
